If you think the Wizard is a pushover, try dealing with him without a
wand of death or some means of dealing massive damage, like I did for
the first time in a recent game.  I was playing a Priest, and was
using a flail I'd picked up early in the game, enchanted to +5 (used
to be +6 before a run-in with a disenchanter), with a ring of increase
damage +4 on the side.  Together they weren't enough to finish him off
in a hit or two, so he just kept teleporting away and returning after
healing himself out of the critical range.  I was casting magic
missile at level 30, high enough for it to do some serious hurt, but I
missed him probably two-thirds of the time.  Pretty much the only way
I managed to kill him was to get lucky by hitting him twice with the
same spell, rebounded off a wall.  Still, he lasted long enough to
double-trouble at least twice per appearance, so the pain just went on
and on.

Not only that, but he also came back from death much more rapidly than
I was used to.  The first time was on the vibrating-square level,
before I'd found the square (big mistake on my part).  After a long
fight I dispatched him and his doubles, and he came back again before
I could find the square; another lengthy fight ensued.  He came back
AGAIN in Moloch's Sanctum, where his summoned nasties teamed up with
the existing monsters and overwhelmed me.  Man, that SUCKED.  Monsters
swarmed around me so thickly that often, when I teleported some away,
I only managed a single step before being surrounded again.


